  "finding": "Oceanica now suppresses supplemental outcomes when the original chain effect is negated. Original activation negation already suppressed the callback and is retained. Three original Harmony own-Hand cases and nine original Bobbie recovery cases verify effect/activation negation, actual Deck/GY-to-Hand recovery before either bottom choice, receiver Normal/Special mode, decline/no-resource and Skill Drain Hand-effect exception. Exact prior source fails one effect-negated case in each family; wrong handler-status guard fails the Hand/Skill Drain exception and fails to suppress chain negation. Omitted recovery/bottom independently fail all five successful recovery cases. Twenty-eight prior complete-current-source aura/ownership/followup regressions pass under distinct output names.",
  "qualification": "Explicit test-only missing-query mapping observes actual native EVENT_CHAIN_DISABLED, clears at CHAIN_END and supplies IsChainDisabled only for this chain-solved diagnostic. It changes no effects/outcomes and does not prove the original getter in native Omega. Unadapted public failure preserved; native query compatibility remains open. Complete original Oceanica/Harmony/Bobbie metadata and effects, neutral counter/recipient/bottom supports; no replacement source effect or recipe. No full-card/live Omega certification.",
  "remaining": "Eligibility/selection when a source effect summons from both players hands remains unresolved; this proves a valid original Bobbie recovery path, not complete additional-mode choice coverage. Original IsChainDisabled native/runtime verification and other integrations remain open."
